+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias at module level or in a class. The optional
+   ``canonical`` option describes the type represented by the alias and is
+   displayed in the signature after an equals sign. The expression is parsed
+   as a Python annotation, so referenced types use normal cross-reference
+   resolution. A description body may be provided.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      The type represented by the alias. It is optional; aliases without it
